WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.601
-Our next guest has her comedy
album, "Salt Daddy,"

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.167
available on Apple Music.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:07.868
Making her television debut,

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:10.601
please welcome the very funny
Katherine Blanford.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:26.501
-Oh! This is so cool!

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.634
Oh, my God!

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:30.801
Especially because I grew up
a weird kid,

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:34.033
and my parents wanted me
to be normal so bad.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.133
So they made me pick a sport.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:37.767
So I picked cross-country

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.334
'cause it was the closest thing
to being a horse.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.601
It was a thing.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:46.367
And then, a mile into
every race, I would remember,

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.701
"Oh, I hate running.

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.767
I'm more of a show pony."
Right?

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:53.667
So, I would fake pass out.

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.000
I got really good at it.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.834
I would do a
couple little lazy twirls,

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.467
and then, on the way down,

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:02.534
I'd grab a girl's hair
for witness.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.868
"Remember me."

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.868
And my mom got worried.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.033
She was like, "Katherine,
I'm going to take you

00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:11.901
to see a cardiologist
for your fainting,"

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.601
because my mother
believed in me too much.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.567
And I didn't tell her
I was faking it.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:21.067
I let them run
hours of tests on me.

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:24.834
And then this sweet little heart
doctor told my mother and I

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.901
that I was his first patient
that he ever diagnosed

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.801
with a personality disorder.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:33.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:37.367
Don't clap. Don't clap.

00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:41.334
Here's the best part, though.
He still gave me an inhaler.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.400
He was like, "I don't know.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.767
It could be allergies,
but it's probably narcissism.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.167
Now go ahead.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.167
Go ahead, take a little
puff of this air milk

00:01:59.167 --> 00:02:00.634
every time you're having
a hard time

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:04.334
not being
the center of attention."

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:05.901
And then I just became
an inhaler kid.

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.234
And inhalers are good.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.767
They help you not lose
your breath or your virginity.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.901
So it was a hard childhood.

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:14.167
But now I'm doing great.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.834
I'm too cute -- I'm too cute
to be doing comedy.

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.200
I should be selling
medical equipment.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:23.834
Before comedy,
though, I was a nanny,

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:26.868
because I'm passionate about
eating rich people's food.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:30.667
And sometimes, the parents would
make comments about

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.000
how quickly the fridge emptied.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.934
And I was like, "Oh, okay.
Hold on.

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:35.634
First of all, you don't know
how hard it is to be

00:02:35.634 --> 00:02:37.767
a stay-at-your-home mother."

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:41.234
And they were a wealthy family
in the South,

00:02:41.234 --> 00:02:44.033
so all their kids
were named after nature.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.968
I had a Lily, I had a Forrest,

00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.367
and I had a Treasure Map III.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.634
Yeah, I was
a great nanny, though,

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.567
because I learned from
having a great mom.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.834
And I love talking about my mom.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.133
She passed away
when I was 22 years old.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:58.901
It's hard to say
a joke after this now

00:02:58.901 --> 00:03:01.300
because people are thinking
it's sad that I'm older than 22

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.567
and I still dress like this.

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:10.234
I dress like a
male figure skater from 1994.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.801
But I still hear from my mom.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.334
You know, I don't know if
you've ever gotten a sign

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.534
from up above,
but the other day,

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:21.534
I was driving down
the interstate,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:27.067
just scrolling through
Instagram...

00:03:27.067 --> 00:03:29.868
and I saw this ad for
discounted Botox.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:33.667
So I just commented, "Ugh!
Okay, Mom!"

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:40.234
'Cause my mom was a nurse for
a plastic surgeon.

00:03:40.234 --> 00:03:41.968
And when I was a teenager,

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.300
my mother told me
I needed Botox,

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.334
because sometimes
a mother's touch hurts.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:49.501
And she would come home with

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.601
these little vials of
expired Botox,

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:54.000
and then she would chase me

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.367
around the
house with a syringeful.

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:59.300
Yeah, it was our little game.
We called it freeze tag.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:08.534
Instead of counting to 10,

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:11.767
you just stay frozen
for three to four months.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.133
But I am obsessed with
Instagram.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:15.167
My friends and I -- we're
obsessed with those influencers

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:17.067
that'll go to Tulum, Mexico,

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:18.701
and they'll take
a yacht excursion.

00:04:18.701 --> 00:04:20.000
So we were like,
"We've got to do that."

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.267
So we put all of
our money together

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.701
and we went...
to Fort Lauderdale.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.634
And we wanted to take
a yacht excursion,

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.100
so we found a man
on Craigslist to take us

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:34.300
on his pontoon into the ocean,
where you can't run away.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.601
And that does sound sketchy,

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.868
but we knew we were safe because
his name was Salt Daddy.

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:41.634
So we knew he had daughters.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.100
I know.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.534
He was great.

00:04:49.534 --> 00:04:52.000
He poured us drinks
and he played us music,

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.701
and we did what good little
white girls are supposed to do.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:57.234
We were twerking to Tim McGraw.

00:04:58.534 --> 00:04:59.801
And we were feeling so cute

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:02.467
because Salt Daddy
was taking a lot of videos.

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.734
Just being a classic dad,
you know,

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:09.434
filming all the proud moments
on his iPad.

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:12.267
And then, right at that moment,
this huge boat pulled up,

00:05:12.267 --> 00:05:14.901
and it was full of these
just gorgeous women.

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:17.701
And Salt Daddy was about to
get on their boat.

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:18.801
And I
realized -- I was like, "Wait.

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:21.334
I'm not ready for
a new mom yet."

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:25.567
So I pulled my best move
and I fake passed out.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:30.434
But on the way down,
I for real fell overboard.

00:05:30.434 --> 00:05:32.267
And as I was going under,

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.501
I could hear everybody
shouting my name.

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:37.367
And I saw Salt Daddy dive in
to save me.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:39.901
And my lungs started to
fill up with water,

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:41.667
and then my heart
started to fill up with

00:05:41.667 --> 00:05:44.667
all the attention I was getting.

00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:46.000
And that's when I realized,

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.634
"Oh, I should have joined
the swim team."

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:53.334
Thank you so much.
I've been Katherine Blanford.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:56.868
♪♪

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:58.200
-She believed in you too much.
-Thank you so much.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:01.434
-I love that.
Katherine Blanford!

00:06:01.434 --> 00:06:03.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
Katherine Blanford!

00:06:03.567 --> 00:06:06.968
"Salt Daddy"
is available on Apple Music.

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:08.634
We'll be right back, everybody.

